### II. ARCHITECTURAL SUMMARY OF THE FIX

The patch amends **Article 4.5.2** via four interlocking structural mechanisms:
1. **Anti-Agnotological Sponsoring Threshold (20%):** A dissenting vote is legally void unless co-sponsored by at least twenty percent (20%) of seated delegates and accompanied by a thermodynamically certified alternative plan. This prevents bad-faith single-delegate obstruction and model flooding.
2. **Deterministic Condorcet Rank-Choice Optimization:** If an assembly deadlocks across two successive ballots separated by fourteen (14) days, it immediately initiates pairwise Condorcet rank-choice optimization across all verified plans to map preference transitivity.
3. **Compressed Arbitral Run-Off via Sortition Circuit-Breaker:** The overall deadlock horizon is compressed from ninety (90) to sixty (60) days. If deadlock persists, an auxiliary Synthesis Jury of one hundred and one (101) citizens—maintaining strict odd parity—is empaneled to resolve the dispute within fourteen (14) days via a binding simple majority (50%+1) run-off between the top two Condorcet finalists. Because the jury contains an odd number of delegates, mathematical parity deadlock is impossible.
4. **Telemetric Baseline Continuity ($B_0$):** Operational physical flows continue uninterrupted under the preceding baseline allocation calibrated to empirical sensor telemetry. The amendment explicitly bars legislative deliberative deadlocks from tripping acute safe-mode triage.

